<!-- The sixteen blends (docs/spec/blends.md), each over a box below it, for two pairs of colours. Each cell is 30 by 10:
     the box below at its left, 20 wide; the blended box from x = 10, 20 wide; the overlap from 10 to 19. Rows 0 to 3 hold
     pair A (the element #cc3399 over #669933), rows 4 to 7 pair B (#33ff66 over #cc00ff), four blends to a row in the
     notation's order. Each pair stands in a parent <box> with mix-blend-mode="lighten": a blend other than normal draws the
     parent with its children apart, over a clear backdrop, as CSS's stacking context does, so outside the overlap each box
     keeps its own colour; lighten then lays the parent over the black frame unchanged (the greater of 0 and each channel).
     The last row holds multiply of pair A at an opacity of 0.6 in such a parent, and multiply of pair A with no parent,
     which mixes with the black frame where the blended box is alone. 120 by 90 pixels, 10 frames a second. -->
